# Cases that need images: their streams carry sixel strings or kitty graphics
# commands, or their replies say sixel is on (DA1 attribute 4). A libtsm built
# with -Dimages=false (ADR-103 in aaronsb/kmscon, libtsm's images option) has
# neither, so check.py --no-images leaves these out; every other case in
# cases.list replays against the same golden in both builds. A name followed
# by "replies" differs only in its replies: check.py --no-images compares its
# other lines (size, cursor, flags, rows, checkpoints) with the golden.
